    {
      "title": "Investments by PE/VC funds jump to $4.1 billion in July: Report",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/investments-by-pe-vc-funds-jump-to-4-1-billion-in-july-report-126083100792_1.html",
      "description": "Private equity and venture capital funds' investments in India increased 3 per cent year-on-year to USD 4.1 billion in July, as per a report released on Monday.\nThe investments were up from USD 4 billion recorded in July last year, and 52 per cent higher than USD 2.7 billion invested in the preceding month, the report by the consultant EY and industry grouping IVCA said.\nThe number of deals in July 2026 at 111 was 7 per cent lower than the 119 transactions in July 2025, indicating a jump in ticket sizes, and were much higher than the 80 deals in June 2026, the report said.\n\"India's macroeconomic fundamentals remain supportive of investment activity. With significant dry powder available across PE/VC (Private equity and venture capital) funds, deal-making is expected to accelerate further as geopolitical conditions stabilise,\" the consultancy firm's partner Vivek Soni said.\nJuly 2026 recorded 10 large deals totaling USD 2.8 billion or around 68 per cent of the total activity, it sai",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-31T13:14:44"
    }
